    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1// check whether a student passed or failed the exam.\n2// we will assume the passing grade is 50 or more.\n3\n4#include <iostream>\n5using namespace std;\n6\n7int main() {\n8\n9    int student_grade;\n10  \n11    // get student score from the user\n12    cout << \"Enter grade: \";\n13    cin >> student_grade;\n14\n15    // if grade is 50 or above, student_grade >= results to true\n16    if (student_grade >= 50) {\n17        cout << \"Congratulations!\" << endl;\n18        cout << \"You passed the examination.\";\n19    }\n20  \n21    return 0;\n22}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sample Output 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Enter grade: 72\nCongratulations!\nYou passed the examination."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If the user enters 72, student_grade >= 50 in the if statement will be true. In this case, the statements inside the if block are executed."
    },
